[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
In order to start using clamav-unofficial-sigs, you need to configure
it first. Sample configuration files have been installed to:

%%ETCDIR%%

All user configuration changes should go in file "user.conf". Modify
it according to your needs and when you are done set the value of
"user_configuration_complete" parameter to "yes".

To run the script periodically by cron, you also need to add it to
your crontab.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  maximum_version: "7.99"
  message: <<EOM
clamav-unofficial-sigs 8.0.0 ships a new master.conf (config_version 100).

master.conf is not meant to be edited. If your copy differs from the
installed sample it was left in place and still carries the 7.x defaults.
Keep your changes in user.conf and replace master.conf with the new
sample:

  cp %%ETCDIR%%/master.conf.sample %%ETCDIR%%/master.conf

The script's own --upgrade option is disabled in this package; upgrade
with "mport upgrade" instead.

Behavior changes in 8.0.0:
- The Yara-Rules project databases are now disabled by default. With
  remove_disabled_databases="yes" (the default) their files are removed
  from the ClamAV database directory on the next run. Set
  yararulesproject_enabled="yes" in user.conf to keep them.
- The free MalwarePatrol product code is now 32. If user.conf still sets
  malwarepatrol_product_code="8", change it to "32".
- New optional sources ditekshen and twinclams are available (disabled
  by default).
EOM
}
]
